**SofaBaton X Series Local Integration Specification**

_Generic Local Control Protocol: mDNS Service Discovery, MQTT Messaging & Key ID Mapping_

# 1\. Architecture & General Principles

This technical document outlines the local control and integration interface for the SofaBaton Hub (X Series). Designed for third-party smart home controllers and hubs (such as Hubitat Elevation, Home Assistant, Homebridge, etc.), the architecture operates entirely over the local network using zero-configuration mDNS discovery and standard MQTT messaging.

**Conventions & Communication Standards:  
**• Transport: Local MQTT broker; all payloads are formatted as standard UTF-8 JSON.  
• Device Identifier ({mac}): 12-character hexadecimal MAC address without delimiters (e.g., AABBCCDDEEFF).  
• Message Flow:  
\- Controller -> Hub (Command/Query): Published by the smart home platform; subscribed by the Hub.  
\- Hub -> Controller (Status/Event): Published by the Hub; subscribed by the smart home platform.

# 2\. Network Discovery (mDNS)

The Hub advertises its presence on the local subnet via Multicast DNS (mDNS) over UDP:

**Service Type:** \_sofabaton_hub.\_udp.

Sample mDNS TXT Record:

```
{
  "NO": "xxxxx",
  "NAME": "Living Room Hub",
  "AVER": "1.2.0",
  "HVER": "1.0",
  "MAC": "AABBCCDDEEFF"
}
```

**TXT Record Fields:  
**• NO: Hardware batch / serial identifier.  
• NAME: Hub broadcast / user-friendly display name.  
• AVER: Application firmware version.  
• HVER: Hardware version.  
• MAC: 12-character physical device address.

# 3\. Activity Management

An Activity represents a multi-device operational state (e.g., 'Watch Apple TV', 'Play PS5'). The controller can query activities, trigger state changes, and receive real-time updates when an activity is started or stopped.

## 3.1 Request Activity List

**• Topic:** activity/{mac}/list_request  
**• Direction:** Controller -> Hub

```
{
  "data": "activity_list"
}
```

## 3.2 Report Activity List

**• Topic:** activity/{mac}/list  
**• Direction:** Hub -> Controller

```
{
  "data": [
    {
      "activity_id": 1,
      "activity_name": "Watch TV",
      "state": "off"
    },
    {
      "activity_id": 2,
      "activity_name": "Play Game",
      "state": "on"
    },
    {
      "activity_id": 3,
      "activity_name": "Listen to Music",
      "state": "off"
    }
  ],
  "activity_count": 3
}
```

## 3.3 Control Activity State (Command Down)

Used by the controller to switch an activity ON or OFF.**• Topic:** activity/{mac}/activity_control_down  
**• Direction:** Controller -> Hub

```
{
  "data": {
    "activity_id": 1,
    "state": "on"
  }
}
```

## 3.4 Activity State Feedback (Status Up)

Broadcasted by the Hub whenever an activity state changes (via the remote, mobile app, or smart home commands).**• Topic:** activity/{mac}/activity_control_up  
**• Direction:** Hub -> Controller

```
{
  "data": {
    "activity_id": 1,
    "state": "off"
  }
}
```

**Recommended Driver State Synchronization:  
**1\. Activity Switching: When switching from Activity A to Activity B, the Hub reports the activity_id of the newly activated activity. The controller driver should mark that activity as active/on, and ensure all other activities are set to off.  
2\. Global Power OFF: When the physical 'Power Off' key is pressed, the Hub sends activity_id: 255 (0xFF). The controller should treat this as a global turn-off event and mark all activity devices as off.

